 "version": 1,
 "title": "Rave Stab",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: the bright, short chord stab of early-90s rave, acid and techno: play a chord and it hits and dies away into a little room.\n\nHow it's built: per voice, two saws a few cents apart and a pulse an octave up, through the Ladder filter; one envelope sweeps the filter shut quickly, another shapes the volume (no sustain: a stab). Then Chorus for width and Reverb for the room. Six voices for chords.\n\nPlay: minor chords and minor sevenths, in rhythm.\n\nTweak: the filter envelope's DECAY (shorter is snappier), the filter's CUTOFF and CV, the reverb's SIZE and MIX.",
